.         predict pc1_Support_Gender_Equality, score
(5 components skipped)

Scoring coefficients 
    sum of squares(column-loading) = 1

    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
        Variable |    Comp1     Comp2     Comp3     Comp4     Comp5     Comp6 
    -------------+------------------------------------------------------------
    Support_Ge~1 |   0.4565   -0.1375   -0.1648    0.0966   -0.7319    0.4479 
    Support_Ge~2 |   0.4881   -0.2303   -0.1482    0.0191   -0.1182   -0.8200 
    Support_Ge~3 |   0.4335   -0.2096   -0.2533    0.5017    0.6084    0.2866 
    Support_Ge~4 |   0.2297    0.8998   -0.3664   -0.0053    0.0234   -0.0533 
    Support_Ge~5 |   0.3530    0.2621    0.8633    0.2475    0.0007   -0.0139 
    Support_Ge~6 |   0.4338   -0.0763    0.0847   -0.8230    0.2823    0.2044 
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------

.         
.         * Generate controls
.         // Gender of the respondent
.         rename sex Gender

.         // Age of the respondent
.         g Age=syear-gebjahr

.         // Marital Status of the respondent
.         g Marital_Status=pgfamstd if pgfamstd>0
(1,570 missing values generated)

.         // Employment status
.         rename pgemplst Employment_Status

.         // Income (Net)
.         g Income_Net=pglabnet if pglabnet>=0
(150,526 missing values generated)

.         replace Income_Net=0 if pglabnet<0 & Employment_Status==5 // Income_N
> et is assumed to be zero for individuals who are not employed and who did not
>  declaire any income (pglabnet=-2)
(150,524 real changes made)

.         // Education in years
.         g Education_In_Years=pgbilzeit if pgbilzeit>=0
(4,733 missing values generated)

.         // Number of Children up to the observation year
.         g Num_Sons=0

.         forvalues i=1(1)19{
  2.                 qui replace Num_Sons=Num_Sons+1 if kidsex`i'==1
  3.                 }       

.         g Num_Children=Num_Daughters+Num_Sons

.         // Migraation background
.         rename migback Migration_Background

.         // Sample region
.         g Sample_Region=sampreg if sampreg>0
(22 missing values generated)

.         // Religion
.         g Religion=plh0258_h if plh0258_h>0
(271,572 missing values generated)

.         // Parents minimum education level      
.         g Parents_Min_Edu=min(msedu, fsedu) if fsedu>=0 & msedu>=0
(55,641 missing values generated)

.         // Current health
.         g Current_Health=ple0008 if ple0008>0
(452 missing values generated)

. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 *
.         * Verbal description of the model: Support_Gender_Equality = β₀ + β₁ 
> * Having_Daughters + Controls + ε 
.         
.         * We consider a: linear OLS regression
. 
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis (with robust s
> tandard errors) using pc1_Support_Gender_Equality as dependent variable and H
> aving_Daughters, Gender, and Having_Daughters_x_Gender as independent variabl
> es.
.         g Having_Daughters_x_Gender=Having_Daughters*Gender

.         reg pc1_Support_Gender_Equality Having_Daughters Gender Having_Daught
> ers_x_Gender Age Marital_Status Employment_Status Income_Net Education_In_Yea
> rs Num_Children Migration_Background Sample_Region Religion Parents_Min_Edu C
> urrent_Health, vce(robust)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =     13,861
                                                F(14, 13846)      =      79.38
